  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=0$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=0$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
